+# Google APIs — Consume-Side Recipe (NoctusAI)
+
+> **Purpose.** Authoritative consume-side reference for the four shipped
+> Google integration packages under `noctusai_lib.integrations`:
+> **`google_calendar`**, **`google_maps`**, **`youtube`**, **`google_drive`**.
+> A product engineer wiring any of them reads THIS doc. Each ships the full
+> Protocol+Fake+Real+factory shape per `KB § PATTERNS/seed-fake-real-adapter.md`
+> — products consume, never re-implement.
+>
+> **Source of truth:** the four packages' `__init__.py __all__`. Document
+> ONLY exported symbols (verify-the-seed-ships-it).
+>
+> **Gmail is NOT here.** `noctusai_lib.integrations.email` is a Resend-backed
+> digest/invitation sender, not a Gmail client. A real Gmail adapter is an
+> unfilled gap — tracked at `projects/gmail-seed-lift/PROJECT.md`.
+
+---
+
+## 1. `google_calendar` — Calendar v3
+
+### What ships
+
+| Symbol | Kind |
+|---|---|
+| `EventInput`, `EventAttendee`, `CreatedEvent` | value objects |
+| `CalendarAdapter` | **Protocol** — the consume seam |
+| `CalendarCredentialResolver` | **Protocol** — product-injected per-tenant credential lookup |
+| `CalendarCredentials`, `ServiceAccountCalendarCredentials`, `OAuthCalendarCredentials` | credential return shapes |
+| `FakeCalendarAdapter` | **Fake** — deterministic, mirrors Calendar v3 response shape |
+| `get_calendar_adapter(resolver=None, *, tenant_id=None)` | **Factory** |
+| `event_to_google_body`, `google_body_to_created_event`, `parse_google_datetime` | pure mappers |
+
+Real adapters (`GoogleCalendarServiceAccountAdapter`,
+`GoogleCalendarOAuthAdapter`) are **not in `__all__`** — they are selected
+*internally* by the factory from the credential kind. Consumers never
+import them directly; they inject a resolver.
+
+### Consume recipe + auth modes
+
+`resolver is None` → `FakeCalendarAdapter` (dev/test). With a resolver, the
+adapter kind is picked from `resolver.get_credentials(tenant_id)`:
+
+| Credentials returned | Adapter | Auth |
+|---|---|---|
+| `ServiceAccountCalendarCredentials` | service-account adapter | server-to-server; calendar owned/shared/DWD-delegated |
+| `OAuthCalendarCredentials` | OAuth adapter | user-delegated, refresh-token based |
+| `None` | `FakeCalendarAdapter` | safe dev/test fallback |
+
+Real product example —
+`products/imobi-scheduling/backend/app/services/calendar.py:60`:
+
+```python
+from noctusai_lib.integrations.google_calendar import (
+    CalendarAdapter, CalendarCredentials, CreatedEvent,
+    EventAttendee, EventInput,
+)
+# adapter obtained via get_calendar_adapter(resolver, tenant_id=...)
+```
+
+N=2 — `products/therapy-platform/backend/app/services/scheduling/service.py:39`
+(+ `credentials.py:19`, `calendar_sync.py:18`) consume the same surface
+(DRY already formalized at the seed). To drive the scheduling engine, see
+`KB § PATTERNS/scheduling-seed.md`. Google Cloud Console OAuth setup:
+`KB § GUIDES/google-oauth-setup.md`.
+
+---
+
+## 2. `google_maps` — Routes API v2
+
+### What ships
+
+| Symbol | Kind |
+|---|---|
+| `Coordinates`, `TravelEstimate` | value objects |
+| `RoutingAdapter` | **Protocol** |
+| `StaticRoutingAdapter` | **Fake** — deterministic dev/test fallback |
+| `GoogleMapsRoutingAdapter` | **Real** — live Routes API; takes an API key |
+| `get_routing_adapter(api_key=None)` | **Factory** — `api_key` set → real; else `StaticRoutingAdapter` |
+| `build_routes_request`, `parse_routes_response` | pure mappers |
+
+### Consume recipe + auth
+
+API-key auth only (no OAuth). Real product example —
+`products/imobi-scheduling/backend/app/services/maps.py:43`:
+
+```python
+from noctusai_lib.integrations.google_maps import (
+    Coordinates, RoutingAdapter, StaticRoutingAdapter, get_routing_adapter,
+)
+adapter = get_routing_adapter(api_key=settings.google_maps_api_key)
+```
+
+To plug into `noctusai_lib.domain.scheduling.SchedulingEngine`, build a
+product-side `TravelLookup` owning a `location_id → Coordinates` map and
+delegating `travel_minutes(...)` to `RoutingAdapter.travel_estimate(...)`
+— the mapping is product-specific so it stays consumer-side
+(`KB § PATTERNS/scheduling-seed.md`).
+
+---
+
+## 3. `youtube` — Data API v3
+
+### What ships
+
+| Symbol | Kind |
+|---|---|
+| `Channel`, `Video`, `Playlist`, `ListResult[T]` | value objects |
+| `YoutubeClient` | **Protocol** — quota-cost documented per method |
+| `FakeYoutubeClient` | **Fake** — tracks cumulative `quota_units_consumed`; `PAGE_SIZE=2` |
+| `RealYoutubeClient(api_key=, oauth_credentials=)` | **Real** — wraps `googleapiclient` |
+| `make_youtube_client(use_fake=False, api_key=, oauth_credentials=, fake_seed_data=None)` | **Factory** |
+
+### Consume recipe + auth
+
+API key OR `oauth_credentials`. **Quota math is the point of lifting this:**
+`search()` burns 100 units/page; `list_channel_videos()` is ~50× cheaper
+(~2 units / 50 videos via the channel auto-uploads playlist). The Protocol
+docstrings carry the costs — read them and pick the cheap path.
+
+```python
+from noctusai_lib.integrations.youtube import make_youtube_client
+yt = make_youtube_client(api_key=settings.google_api_key)
+```
+
+Current consumer is `youtube-crawler` (a separate workspace product —
+N=1 in `products/`). The seed lift landed ahead of a second consumer
+deliberately ("spread it throughout soon" — user-authorized).
+
+---
+
+## 4. `google_drive` — Drive v3 download
+
+### What ships
+
+| Symbol | Kind |
+|---|---|
+| `DriveFile` | value object (id/name/size_bytes/mime_type/md5_checksum) |
+| `DriveDownloader` | **Protocol** — `get_metadata` + `download` |
+| `FakeDriveDownloader` | **Fake** — `add_fake_file(...)` fixtures; writes seeded bytes |
+| `make_drive_downloader(use_fake=False, api_key=None, oauth_credentials=None, fake_seed_data=None)` | **Factory** |
+| `parse_drive_url(url_or_id)` | pure mapper — accepts `file/d/{id}`, `open?id=`, `uc?id=`, bare ids |
+
+`RealDriveDownloader` is **not in `__all__`** — selected internally by the
+factory.
+
+### Consume recipe + auth
+
+"Anyone with the link" files: `api_key` (cheaper, no consent) OR
+`oauth_credentials` with `drive.readonly`. Private files: OAuth required.
+The Protocol is auth-agnostic; the factory routes.
+
+```python
+from noctusai_lib.integrations.google_drive import (
+    make_drive_downloader, parse_drive_url,
+)
+drive = make_drive_downloader(api_key=settings.google_api_key)
+file_id = parse_drive_url(user_supplied_url)
+await drive.download(file_id, dest=tmp_path / file_id)
+```
+
+Current consumer: `youtube-crawler` upload pipeline (N=1).
+
+---
+
+## 5. Out-of-scope / gaps
+
+- **No Gmail client.** `noctusai_lib.integrations.email` is Resend digest +
+  invitation only. A `noctusai_lib.integrations.gmail` Protocol+Fake+Real+
+  factory does NOT exist — required before any `google.gmail.*` surface.
+  Tracked: `projects/gmail-seed-lift/PROJECT.md` (Filed, not started).
+- **Calendar/Drive real adapters are factory-internal** — not in `__all__`
+  by design; inject a resolver / pass credentials, never import the real
+  class.
+- **youtube + google_drive are N=1** (`youtube-crawler` only). Seed-lifted
+  ahead of the second consumer per explicit user authorization — not a
+  recurrence-rule violation.
+- Cross-provider OAuth model (scope auto-discovery, credential store,
+  token chains) is documented at `KB § INTEGRATIONS/oauth-patterns.md` —
+  read it before designing any new Google OAuth wiring.
+
+---
+
+## 6. Change log
+
+| Date | Change | By |
+|---|---|---|
+| 2026-05-17 | Initial consume-side authoring (`mcp-connector-expansion` Wave 1b). Closes social-wiring-absorption consume-doc debt. Surfaces verified against the four packages' `__init__.py __all__`; product consumers cited at exact `path:line` (imobi-scheduling calendar.py:60 + maps.py:43; therapy-platform scheduling/service.py:39). Gmail gap filed as `gmail-seed-lift`. | Claude Opus 4.7 |
