+# Meta Cloud API — Consume-Side Recipe (NoctusAI)
+
+> **Purpose.** Authoritative consume-side reference for the seed Meta
+> integration. **Scope alert (verify-the-seed-ships-it):** there is **no
+> standalone `noctusai_lib.integrations.meta` package**. The only Meta
+> surface that ships today is the **Meta WhatsApp Cloud API outbound text
+> client**, which lives **inside** `noctusai_lib.integrations.whatsapp`
+> (`MetaCloudClient` / `FakeMetaCloudClient` / `get_meta_cloud_client`).
+> This doc documents what actually exists, not the broader Graph API.
+>
+> A product engineer wiring Meta WhatsApp sending reads THIS doc + the
+> sibling connector doc `KB § INTEGRATIONS/whatsapp.md`. The seed already
+> ships the full Fake+Real+factory shape — products consume, never
+> re-implement.
+>
+> **Source of truth:** `seed/lib/backend/noctusai_lib/integrations/whatsapp/meta_cloud_client.py`
+> + the package `__init__.py __all__`.
+
+---
+
+## 1. What ships
+
+| Symbol | Kind | Notes |
+|---|---|---|
+| `MetaCloudClient(phone_number_id, api_key, base_url=DEFAULT)` | **Real** | Async `send_text(phone, text) -> dict` only. POSTs to `{base_url}/{phone_number_id}/messages`. Raises `httpx.HTTPStatusError` on non-2xx — consumer catches + shapes. |
+| `FakeMetaCloudClient(phone_number_id=None, base_url=DEFAULT)` | **Fake** | Deterministic in-memory. Records `sent_messages`; returns canonical envelope `{"messaging_product": "whatsapp", "contacts": [...], "messages": [{"id": "fake-meta-<N>"}]}`. `clear()` resets between test cases. |
+| `get_meta_cloud_client(*, phone_number_id=None, api_key=None, base_url=META_CLOUD_DEFAULT_BASE_URL)` | **Factory** | `api_key` set → `MetaCloudClient`; else `FakeMetaCloudClient`. |
+| `META_CLOUD_DEFAULT_BASE_URL` | constant | `https://graph.facebook.com/v18.0`. |
+
+All four are re-exported from
+`noctusai_lib.integrations.whatsapp.__all__` — import from the **package**,
+not the submodule:
+
+```python
+from noctusai_lib.integrations.whatsapp import get_meta_cloud_client
+```
+
+There is **no Protocol class for Meta** — `MetaCloudClient` and
+`FakeMetaCloudClient` are structurally compatible (both expose
+`async send_text(phone, text) -> dict`); the factory returns the union
+type `MetaCloudClient | FakeMetaCloudClient`. The shared seam Protocol
+for WhatsApp at large is `WhatsAppClient` (see `KB § INTEGRATIONS/whatsapp.md`).
+
+---
+
+## 2. Consume recipe
+
+The `api_key`-set switch IS the configured-vs-not signal. Meta rejects all
+unauthenticated requests, so an unset key MUST route to the Fake —
+the factory enforces this; consumers never branch on environment.
+
+### Real product example
+
+`products/erp-imobiliario/backend/app/services/whatsapp_service.py:196`
+wraps the factory in a thin product-specific service (ERP-specific
+envelope parsing stays product-side; the HTTP/auth/body shaping lives
+in the seed `MetaCloudClient`):
+
+```python
+from noctusai_lib.integrations.whatsapp import get_meta_cloud_client
+
+client = get_meta_cloud_client(
+    phone_number_id=settings.meta_phone_number_id,
+    api_key=settings.meta_api_key,   # unset in dev → FakeMetaCloudClient
+)
+resp = await client.send_text(phone, body)   # phone = international digits-only
+```
+
+Mount any inbound webhook through the seed router seam — see
+`KB § INTEGRATIONS/whatsapp.md § 2b` (`create_whatsapp_webhook_router`,
+mounted via the seed app factory `routers=[...]` seam, not hand-written).
+
+**Recipient addressing differs from WAHA.** `MetaCloudClient.send_text`
+takes a **phone** (international digits-only, no `+`), NOT the WAHA
+`<digits>@c.us` chat-id. Do not pass `chat_id_for_phone(...)` output to
+the Meta client.
+
+---
+
+## 3. Auth modes
+
+| Mode | When | Shape |
+|---|---|---|
+| **System-user / app Bearer token** | `api_key` set | `Authorization: Bearer <api_key>` header (set by `MetaCloudClient._headers`). `phone_number_id` selects the sending WhatsApp Business number. |
+| **Fake (no auth)** | `api_key` unset | `FakeMetaCloudClient` — deterministic, no network. Dev/test default. |
+
+There is no OAuth flow in this client — the token is a long-lived
+Meta system-user / app access token resolved from product settings.
+Broader Meta OAuth (Pages / Ads / Instagram token chains, scope
+auto-discovery, post-consent introspection) is documented separately at
+`KB § INTEGRATIONS/oauth-patterns.md` (the cross-provider OAuth model) —
+but **no Graph-API client consuming that exists in the seed today**.
+
+Inbound webhook signature verification (Meta `X-Hub-Signature-256`) is
+the webhook layer's job — `KB § PATTERNS/webhook-signatures.md`
+(Hub-Signature shape) + the 5-pin verify-before-side-effect contract in
+`create_whatsapp_webhook_router`.
+
+---
+
+## 4. Out-of-scope / gaps
+
+- **WhatsApp Cloud outbound TEXT only.** No media send, no template
+  messages, no inbound parsing in `MetaCloudClient` itself — inbound lands
+  later under the shared `WhatsAppInboundMessage` shape
+  (`KB § PATTERNS/whatsapp-chatbot-seed.md §1`).
+- **No general Meta Graph API client.** There is NO Pages / Ads / Instagram
+  / Marketing-API / Insights client in the seed. If a product needs Graph
+  read (page insights, ad metrics, IG content) that is a **new seed module**
+  (`noctusai_lib.integrations.meta`) to be filed Protocol+Fake+Real+factory —
+  it does not exist yet. The brief-era framing "Meta = read-only v1, no
+  posting/ads" does NOT describe a shipped surface; only WhatsApp-send ships.
+- **No `meta` package.** Anything that imports
+  `from noctusai_lib.integrations.meta import ...` is wrong — the symbols
+  live under `...integrations.whatsapp`.
+
+---
+
+## 5. Change log
+
+| Date | Change | By |
+|---|---|---|
+| 2026-05-17 | Initial consume-side authoring (`mcp-connector-expansion` Wave 1b). Surface verified against `whatsapp/meta_cloud_client.py` + `whatsapp/__init__.py __all__`. **Finding surfaced:** no standalone `meta` package — the only Meta surface is WhatsApp Cloud outbound text inside the whatsapp package; doc documents the real shape and flags the absent Graph-API client as a gap. Consumer cited at `erp-imobiliario/.../whatsapp_service.py:196`. | Claude Opus 4.7 |
