+# WhatsApp Connector — Consume-Side Recipe (NoctusAI)
+
+> **Purpose.** Authoritative consume-side reference for the seed WhatsApp
+> connector `noctusai_lib.integrations.whatsapp`. A product engineer wiring
+> inbound/outbound WhatsApp reads THIS doc; the seed already ships the whole
+> Protocol+Fake+Real+factory shape — products consume, never re-implement.
+>
+> **Provider-neutral by design.** The public surface is named `WhatsApp*`,
+> not `Waha*` (legacy `Waha*` aliases preserved for the original consumer).
+> Two real backends ship: **WAHA** (self-hosted WhatsApp HTTP API) and
+> **Meta Cloud API** (Meta-hosted WhatsApp Business). Swapping backends does
+> not rename the public surface — see also `KB § INTEGRATIONS/meta.md` for the
+> Meta Cloud client specifics.
+>
+> **Lifted** 2026-05-03 from `whatsapp-google-scheduling/app/services/waha/`
+> via `projects/whatsapp-seed-absorption/`. Canonical wiring recipe (chatbot
+> framework + Redis buffer/worker) lives at `KB § PATTERNS/whatsapp-chatbot-seed.md`;
+> THIS doc is the connector-only consume contract.
+
+---
+
+## 1. What ships
+
+Verified against `seed/lib/backend/noctusai_lib/integrations/whatsapp/__init__.py`
+`__all__` — document ONLY exported symbols (verify-the-seed-ships-it).
+
+### Value objects / types
+
+| Symbol | Role |
+|---|---|
+| `WhatsAppInboundMessage` | Parsed inbound message (sender phone, text, media ref). |
+| `WhatsAppMedia` | Inbound media descriptor (resolve bytes via the client). |
+| `WhatsAppPayloadError` | Raised when the inbound webhook body is unparseable. |
+| `WhatsAppIgnoredEvent` | Non-message webhook event (status callbacks, etc.) — not an error; the router skips it. |
+| `WhatsAppClient` | **Protocol** — the consume seam. Code against this, never a concrete class. |
+| `WhatsAppSettings` | Pydantic settings model (base_url / api_key / session). |
+
+Legacy aliases (original consumer compat — same objects):
+`WahaInboundMessage`, `WahaMedia`, `WahaPayloadError`, `WahaIgnoredEvent`.
+
+### Parsing / shaping (pure functions)
+
+| Symbol | Behavior |
+|---|---|
+| `parse_waha_inbound_message(body)` | WAHA webhook JSON → `WhatsAppInboundMessage` (or raises `WhatsAppPayloadError` / signals `WhatsAppIgnoredEvent`). |
+| `chat_id_for_phone(phone)` | Phone → WAHA chat-id form (`<digits>@c.us`). |
+| `phone_from_chat_id(chat_id)` | Inverse of `chat_id_for_phone`. |
+| `build_send_text_body(...)` | Build the outbound send-text request body. |
+
+### Adapters
+
+| Symbol | Kind | When |
+|---|---|---|
+| `WahaClient` | **Real** (WAHA HTTP) | `base_url` set → real self-hosted WAHA server. Sync + async `send_text` + `download_media`. |
+| `MetaCloudClient` | **Real** (Meta Cloud) | `api_key` set → Meta-hosted Business API. See `KB § INTEGRATIONS/meta.md`. |
+| `FakeWahaClient` | **Fake** | Default. Bi-directional in-memory: records `sent_messages`, accepts `inject_text` / `inject_inbound`, serves pre-populated `media_bytes`. |
+| `FakeMetaCloudClient` | **Fake** | Default for the Meta path. |
+| `META_CLOUD_DEFAULT_BASE_URL` | constant | Default Meta Graph base URL. |
+
+### Factory + FastAPI
+
+| Symbol | Role |
+|---|---|
+| `get_whatsapp_client(*, base_url=None, api_key=None, session="default")` | WAHA factory. `base_url` set → `WahaClient`; else `FakeWahaClient`. Mirrors `google_calendar.get_calendar_adapter()` per `KB § PATTERNS/seed-fake-real-adapter.md`. |
+| `get_meta_cloud_client(*, phone_number_id=None, api_key=None, base_url=META_CLOUD_DEFAULT_BASE_URL)` | Meta Cloud factory. `api_key` set → `MetaCloudClient`; else `FakeMetaCloudClient`. |
+| `create_whatsapp_webhook_router(...)` | FastAPI router **factory** — builds the inbound-webhook receiver. |
+| `InboundHandler` | The callback Protocol the router invokes per parsed inbound message. |
+
+---
+
+## 2. Consume recipe
+
+The `base_url`-set / `api_key`-set switch IS the configured-vs-not signal —
+no env in dev/test → Fake, transparently. Consumers never branch on
+"is this a test"; they call the factory and inject credentials from settings.
+
+### 2a. Outbound (WAHA) — real product example
+
+`products/erp-imobiliario/backend/app/services/whatsapp_service.py:336` —
+the ERP wraps the WAHA factory in a thin product-specific service:
+
+```python
+from noctusai_lib.integrations.whatsapp import get_whatsapp_client
+
+client = get_whatsapp_client(
+    base_url=settings.waha_base_url,   # unset in dev → FakeWahaClient
+    api_key=settings.waha_api_key,
+    session=settings.waha_session,
+)
+await client.send_text(chat_id_for_phone(phone), body)
+```
+
+`products/therapy-platform/backend/app/services/whatsapp_therapy_service.py:63`
+consumes the same factory (N=2 — DRY-formalized at the seed already).
+
+### 2b. Inbound webhook — mount via the NAMED router seam
+
+The router is NOT hand-written per product. `imobi-scheduling` mounts the
+seed factory through the seed router seam
+(`products/imobi-scheduling/backend/app/routers/whatsapp_router.py:55`):
+
+```python
+from noctusai_lib.integrations.whatsapp import (
+    WhatsAppInboundMessage,
+    WhatsAppSettings,
+    create_whatsapp_webhook_router,
+)
+
+_seed_router = create_whatsapp_webhook_router(
+    settings=WhatsAppSettings(...),
+    handler=my_inbound_handler,        # implements InboundHandler
+)
+router.include_router(_seed_router, prefix="/api/webhooks/whatsapp")
+```
+
+The product router is registered via the seed app factory `routers=[...]`
+seam — `products/imobi-scheduling/backend/app/main.py:39`
+(`standard_routers=["health", "notificacoes", "team"]` + the custom
+whatsapp router). No `create_product_app` bypass.
+
+### 2c. Meta Cloud outbound
+
+`products/erp-imobiliario/backend/app/services/whatsapp_service.py:196`
+consumes `get_meta_cloud_client(...)`. Full Meta Cloud surface +
+auth-mode matrix in `KB § INTEGRATIONS/meta.md`.
+
+---
+
+## 3. Auth modes
+
+| Backend | Configured-signal | Auth shape |
+|---|---|---|
+| WAHA (`WahaClient`) | `base_url` non-empty | API key header against the self-hosted WAHA server (`api_key=` → request header). `session` selects the WAHA session. |
+| Meta Cloud (`MetaCloudClient`) | `api_key` non-empty | Bearer token (Meta system-user / app token); `phone_number_id` selects the sending number. Meta rejects all unauthenticated requests — unset key ⇒ `FakeMetaCloudClient`. |
+| Fake (either) | nothing set | No auth; deterministic in-memory. The dev/test default. |
+
+Inbound webhook signature verification is a separate concern — see
+`KB § PATTERNS/webhook-signatures.md` (Hub-Signature shape for Meta;
+WAHA shared-secret). `create_whatsapp_webhook_router` wires the
+verify-before-side-effect 5-pin contract.
+
+---
+
+## 4. Out-of-scope / gaps
+
+- **Provider-neutral, two backends only.** WAHA + Meta Cloud ship. Twilio /
+  other providers are NOT shipped — the Protocol is named to make adding one
+  non-breaking, but no adapter exists yet (N=1 if/when needed).
+- **Connector only.** Message buffering, debounce, the LLM dispatcher, and
+  the chatbot conversation loop are NOT in this package — they live in
+  `noctusai_lib.domain.chatbot` + the Redis worker. Wiring recipe:
+  `KB § PATTERNS/whatsapp-chatbot-seed.md`.
+- **No media transcription here.** Inbound audio/image bytes are resolved
+  via the client (`download_media`); transcription/vision is the LLM layer.
+
+---
