+# gmail-seed-lift — Project Document
+
+> **This is a living document, not a rigid checklist.** As we build and learn,
+> this project document evolves. See `CLAUDE.md → Projects are living documents`.
+>
+> **STATUS: FILED — not started.** Surfaced as a gap by the
+> `mcp-connector-expansion` Wave 1b consume-doc authoring (2026-05-17).
+> No work has begun. Interrogate the user before drafting phases.
+
+- **Created:** 2026-05-17
+- **Last updated:** 2026-05-17
+- **Status:** Filed — not started (gap stub; no design lock; no phases run)
+- **Owner / stakeholders:** joaoraphaelsst@gmail.com
+- **Related docs:** `KB § INTEGRATIONS/google.md` (§5 names this gap) · `KB § INTEGRATIONS/oauth-patterns.md` · `KB § PATTERNS/seed-fake-real-adapter.md` · `KB § PATTERNS/seed-lib-layout.md`
+- **Project slug:** `gmail-seed-lift` — location `projects/gmail-seed-lift/` (cross-product platform-infra: a new seed-lib integration package, not a single-product change). Intent = `seed-lift`.
+
+---
+
+## 1. Context & Purpose
+
+A consume-side audit (`mcp-connector-expansion` Wave 1b, 2026-05-17) found
+that **NoctusAI has no Gmail client in the seed library.**
+`noctusai_lib.integrations.email` is a **Resend-backed** digest +
+invitation sender (`send_product_invitation_email`, `send_digest`,
+`Digest`, `DigestSendResult`) — it is NOT a Gmail API client and shares
+no surface with one. The only Google-auth code that mentions "Gmail" is
+incidental OAuth-scope-example docstrings inside the `google_calendar`
+credential modules.
+
+Any future agent-exposed surface in the shape `google.gmail.*` (read a
+mailbox, send via Gmail, thread/label operations) requires a real seed
+adapter first: per the seed-first contract a product MUST NOT hand-roll a
+Gmail client. The gap is filed here so it is not silently rediscovered.
+
+**Win:** `noctusai_lib.integrations.gmail` ships Protocol+Fake+Real+factory
+mirroring `google_calendar` / `youtube` / `google_drive`, so the first
+Gmail-touching product (and the future `google.gmail.*` MCP surface)
+inherits it instead of forking.
+
+---
+
+## 2. User interrogation (Q → A)
+
+> **Not yet conducted.** Before drafting §6 phases, interrogate the user:
+> - Q: Which product drives the first Gmail need (read inbox / send / both)?
+> - Q: Auth mode — service-account + domain-wide delegation, or per-user
+>   OAuth (`gmail.readonly` / `gmail.send` scopes)?
+> - Q: Read scope (full message bodies — LGPD-sensitive) vs metadata-only?
+> - Q: Is this driven by a concrete project, or pre-emptive seed hardening?
+
+---
+
+## 3. Design principles
+
+1. Mirror the canonical Protocol+Fake+Real+factory shape exactly —
+   `KB § PATTERNS/seed-fake-real-adapter.md`. The Fake must exercise the
+   same code paths the Real does (it is an IO module → not exempt).
+2. Auth-agnostic Protocol; the factory routes api-key / OAuth /
+   service-account, the same way `google_drive` / `google_calendar` do.
+3. LGPD-first: Gmail bodies are personal data. Redaction + consent gating
+   are design inputs, not afterthoughts (`KB § PATTERNS/lgpd.md`).
+
+---
+
+## 3a. Seed-first analysis (REQUIRED)
+
+Six-question checklist (`KB § GUIDES/seed-first-design.md`):
+
+1. **Is the contract identical for every product?** YES — the Gmail API
+   contract is vendor-fixed; every consumer wants the same shapes.
+2. **Is the data source product-specific?** NO — uniform Gmail API; the
+   *credential resolution* is per-tenant (mirrors `CalendarCredentialResolver`).
+3. **Is the placement product-specific?** N/A — this is a seed-lib package,
+   not UI.
+4. **Is the visibility / permission rule the same?** YES — auth-token-gated
+   uniformly; LGPD redaction is a uniform seam.
+5. **Does the seam already exist in seed?** NO — new package
+   `noctusai_lib.integrations.gmail` needed. Adjacent precedent:
+   `google_calendar` (resolver Protocol + factory-internal real adapters),
+   `youtube`/`google_drive` (api_key | oauth factory).
+6. **Default-on or opt-in?** OPT-IN — only products that need Gmail
+   consume the factory; nothing is auto-wired.
+
+**Litmus — per-product code count:** **0 lines** of duplicated client code
+(the whole client lives in seed); a product supplies only a
+credential-resolver + settings (small section, like the calendar consumers).
+
+**Phase plan implications:** §6 phases (when drafted) MUST work entirely in
+`seed/lib/backend/noctusai_lib/integrations/gmail/` + colocated tests.
+**No per-product walk** — if a phase plan iterates products, the design is
+wrong; restart §3a.
+
+---
+
+## 4. Scope
+
+**In scope:**
+- New seed package `noctusai_lib.integrations.gmail`:
+  value objects (message / thread / label shapes), `GmailClient` Protocol,
+  `FakeGmailClient`, real adapter (factory-internal), factory, pure mappers.
+- Colocated tests mirroring `youtube` / `google_drive` test layout.
+- Add to `KB § INTEGRATIONS/google.md` §5 (flip gap → shipped) + three-way
+  sync when it lands.
+
+**Out of scope (for now — with reason):**
+- The `google.gmail.*` MCP tool surface — that is a LATER wave; the seed
+  adapter is the prerequisite (Part B of `mcp-connector-expansion`).
+- Specific product wiring — depends on the §2 interrogation outcome.
+- Push/watch (Pub/Sub) inbound — defer until a concrete product needs it.
+
+---
+
+## 5. Architecture / Data Model
+
+To be designed after the §2 interrogation. Anchor on the existing
+canonical precedents (do NOT re-invent):
+`seed/lib/backend/noctusai_lib/integrations/google_drive/`
+(factory + factory-internal Real + Fake + pure mapper) and
+`.../google_calendar/` (credential-resolver Protocol for per-tenant auth).
+
+---
+
+## 6. Implementation phases
+
+> **Not drafted.** Stub project — phases are authored only after the §2
+> interrogation locks scope + auth mode. Filed so the gap is durable and
+> discoverable, not to prescribe execution.
+
